  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 7b8860589b05b4642ab42b24201a782d, type: 3}
  m_Name: Note_SauerkrautCard
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: GrandmasHouse::GrandmasHouse.Data.NoteData
  kind: 1
  title: Sauerkraut
  recipe: {fileID: 0}
  body: 'Sauerkraut


    Cabbage, sliced on the board

    Salt, a scoop for every
    dozen slices


    Pack the cabbage into the crock down in the cellar a handful
    at a time, and shake the salt over it as you go. Then leave it be. In about a
    week it''s sour and good, and it keeps all winter right there in the crock.


    Scoop
    it into a bowl to eat.'
  marginNote: Skimp on the salt and you'll be feeding it to the chickens.
